
=== S1 Theorem D2(6): explicit instance, closed form, and the leading constant  [0s]
   d=6: lambda_X = 1.000000 (claim 1);  U_y(v*) = 0.707107;  multistart sup|U_y| = 0.707107;  1/sqrt2 = 0.707107
   alpha     max|P_RK4 - P_closed|/P   t_beta(RK4)  t_beta(closed)  T_beta(item 3)  max_{b'<=b} T_b'   ratios t_b*U0/ln(1/a), T_b*U0/ln(1/a), maxT*U0/ln(1/a)   kink |w.x| max, off-v* drift
     1e-01   1.60e-13                    2.5745       2.5745         1.6816          1.6816          0.7906, 0.5164, 0.5164                  0.0e+00, 1.6e-16
     1e-02   4.35e-13                    5.8408       5.8408         4.0873          4.2863          0.8968, 0.6276, 0.6581                  0.0e+00, 1.6e-16
     1e-04   1.46e-12                   12.3536      12.3536         8.8989         10.1869          0.9484, 0.6832, 0.7821                  0.0e+00, 1.6e-16
     1e-08   8.57e-12                   25.3790      25.3790        18.5220         22.6473          0.9742, 0.7110, 0.8694                  0.0e+00, 7.5e-20
   item 3 at fixed beta has limit U0/(U0+lam beta/2) = 0.7388 (beta=0.5); the monotone version max_{beta'<=beta} T_beta' tends to 1,
   so liminf t_beta U0*/ln(1/alpha) >= 1 for every flow, and the instance attains 1: the constant 1/U0* itself is sharp at every fixed beta.

